# The SSH indicator (owner decisions 2026-10-30) on a board with a battery (the FZ-M1 tablet, the HackBerry: the
# harness's fake power_supply, there before the launcher starts as on the board): the glyph takes the place of the
# battery's percentage, which is left out while a session is shown (the level glyph stays), so the strip keeps its width
# at 100 % (640x480 and up) and at 72 % (480x800); the header's Esc stays where "100%" puts it. No session: "85%" as
# before; idle; traffic in both blink phases; charging (green battery, blue glyph); the session ends: "85%" back; the
# Settings root with a session. No header check (another scene's home grid has no battery). Goldens at 640x480 and
# 480x800.
title ssh status battery
sizes 640x480 480x800 720x720 1024x600
@480x800 profile pda
@480x800 env APPLAUNCH_PDA 0
env APPLAUNCH_DEV 0
apps Settings CLI SSH Calculator
clock 20:30
wifi 70
bt on
battery 85 discharging
home
shot ssh_battery_none
ssh_status 1 idle
wait 2100
shot ssh_battery_idle
ssh_status 1 active
wait 2100
shot ssh_battery_active_a
wait 500
shot ssh_battery_active_b
battery 100 charging
ssh_status 1 idle
wait 2100
shot ssh_battery_charging
battery 85 discharging
ssh_status off
wait 2100
expect_same ssh_battery_none
launch Settings
wait 300
shot ssh_battery_settings_none
ssh_status 1 idle
wait 2100
shot ssh_battery_settings
